WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-RU

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.200
Welcome back to the Wheel of Life

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.560
Home Retreat.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.080
I would like to thank Stanley again for the translation.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.080
Thank you for being in America and translating.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.800
We're in lesson 21 and

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:35.720
it's called "Seeing Prison as Prison."  The

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.120
picture shows a prison.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.400
We used to have a very intensive program of training lama rim in prisons.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.720
And it helped the prisoners a lot,

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.520
and the government thanked us because the prisoners started getting into fights less.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.120
The picture you see here is perfect for prison, because

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.920
prison is really depressing.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.440
When we study the Wheel of Life in the monastery,

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.200
we study it from a set of books called sur kel (ZUR BKOL).

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:43.920
There is a tradition of taking about five different subjects

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:52.040
and squeezing specific topics out of the larger books, much like

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.120
you would squeeze medicine out of herbs.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:16.080
And for our computer project to preserve ancient books,

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:25.120
this was the first book we printed,

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.240
and it was called sur kel (ZUR BKOL), five books

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.560
extracted from the big books.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.560
And you will be interested to know,

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:41.960
and we have been studying it for 2-3 months,

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.000
that the entire teaching of the "Wheel of Life",

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.240
as it is taught in the monastery,

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.160
all of it comes from one verse from Maitreya.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.040
More precisely, from one verse, not a stanza.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:13.000
And I think you have heard this verse from me before,

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:23.000
the ne seng khe nam gying pei (DE NAS SENG GE RNAM BSGYINGS PA'I)
ting nge jing la nyom shuk ne (TING NGE 'DZIN LA SNYOMS ZHUGS NAS,)
ten ching drill jung luk thun thang luk mi thun la tok par che (RTEN CING 'BREL 'BYUNG LUGS MTHUN DANG,, LUGS MI MTHUN LA RTOG PAR BYED)

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.480
This teaches both the "Lion Dance"

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.160
and the "Wheel of Life".

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.800
And the part I want to talk about today

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.080
is the final part.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:40.000
It says ten ching drill jung luk thun thang luk mi thun (RTEN CING 'BREL 'BYUNG LUGS MTHUN DANG LUGS MI MTHUN) luk thun thang luk

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.680
mi thun (LUGS MTHUN DANG,,LUGS MI MTHUN) luk thun

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:54.080
(LUGS MTHUN) means one causes two, two causes three, three causes four, etc.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:02.920
The wife in the kitchen says: “I didn’t do anything, and he yelled at me,”

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.120
this is link number one.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.040
Then she screams back.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.640
This is luk thun (LUGS MTHUN), which means the usual order of things

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:20.080
Then luk thun (LUGS MTHUN), which is sometimes called luk dok (LUGS LDOG)

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.520
This means to turn the wheel back,

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.160
to stop the wheel.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:37.000
And you tend to think, oh, it must be, since it's spoken backwards,

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.760
It must go from the twelfth, to the eleventh, to the tenth...

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:47.880
First I die,

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:52.960
then I grow old, then I'm born, then my karma gains weight,

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:56.720
then I weaponize karma,

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.640
I mean, you can have such strange thoughts.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:08.320
But here in the lam rim it is described what it actually means to "spin the wheel back"

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:20.520
the tak luk dok tu khok nyu pey lam shik nyam su len na (DE DAG LUGS LDOG TU 'GOG NUS PA'I LAM ZHIG NYAMS SU LEN NA)

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.920
we follow the Tibetan;

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.480
the tak luk dok tu khok nyu pey lam shik nyam su len na (DE DAG LUGS LDOG TU 'GOG NUS PA'I LAM ZHIG NYAMS SU LEN NA),

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.400
if you embark on a path

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.080
that will give you the opportunity

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:32.760
to stop the Wheel of Life by turning it back.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:43.440
What does it mean to turn the Wheel of Life back, to stop the Wheel of Life?

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:52.080
mar rik pa khak pe thu chye khak (MA RIG PA 'GAG PAS 'DU BYED 'GAGS)

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.240
If you stop misunderstanding, then you stop karma.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:01.360
Let's apply this to the kitchen,

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:04.520
this is where you should apply all your Dharma.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:11.560
If you can't apply it in the kitchen, it's not Dharma.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:22.160
Then if it is Dharma, you can apply it in the kitchen.  Something like that.  There

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:31.480
shouldn't be anything in the 300,000 books on Buddhism that we have that you couldn't find in your kitchen.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:45.080
And if something good or bad happens in the kitchen, it should be described in ancient books.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.000
Because ancient books were written for the kitchen.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:03.600
ma rik pa khak ne thu chiye khak (MA RIG PA 'GAG PAS 'DU BYED 'GAGS)

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:08.000
means if she can stop the

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.680
misunderstanding regarding her husband,

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:18.400
if she doesn't say, "I don't know why he yelled at me,"

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:23.680
but says, "Ah, I know why he yelled at me!

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:29.040
I yelled at my kids last week."

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.680
She just reversed the first link.

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:38.080
She just blocked the first link.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.440
If you block this "I didn't do anything,"

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:48.000
then automatically you won't get to the second link.

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:55.800
"I'm not clueless, you're clueless."

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:57.400
Okay.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:00.680
So if you stop the first link, then the second link will never come.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:06.040
That's how we stop the Wheel of Life.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:11.880
Don't forget that the Wheel of Life is kind of a bad name, a misnomer.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:21.240
It's not really the Wheel of Life.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.640
I mean, Buddha has a life too.

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:29.920
It means the wheel of bad life and the life  full of suffering.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:37.520


00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:41.520
If you stop link #1, you stop link #2.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:49.080
Therefore, you stop all links, including aging and dying. All the pain in your life will

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:57.480


00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.000
be stopped.

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:07.800
And don't think that the Wheel of Life means that if you get off the Wheel of Life, you have to die or disappear.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:17.360
In the Wheel of Life, for example, in the painting,

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:22.760
Buddha is outside the wheel,

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:26.320
and he points to the moon,

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.000
which represents nirvana.

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:33.120
Okay, let's get back to the text.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:38.520
nyon mong duk ngel gyi ten drel sum thu thu te (MDOR BSDU NA, RTEN 'BREL YAN LAG BCU GNYIS LAS DANG NYON MONGS SDUG BSNGAL GYI RTEN 'BREL GSUM DU 'DU STE)

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:42.920
tor du na (MDOR BSDU NA) means, let's summarize

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:48.320
You can take all 12 links

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:59.200
And to summarize, we can divide them a little differently than we did before.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:11.920
We can divide them into number 1 - karma

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:15.920
number 2 - negative thoughts

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:19.880
and number 3 pain.

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:23.440
Okay, you can divide them into these three.

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:29.320
mar rik pa thang se pa len pa sum nyon mong (MA RIG PA DANG, SRED PA, LEN PA GSUM NYON MONGS)

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:32.320
The three links are negative emotions;

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:39.760
This is the misunderstanding of your husband,

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:44.680
And then se pa (SRED PA) we  They said this is a negative coffee meditation. Do

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:49.640
you regret yelling at your husband? No.

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:59.080
Then LEN PA, this is like an advanced negative coffee meditation.

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:08.040
I don't believe there is any connection between yelling at my children and my husband yelling at me.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:19.320
So, these are all three negative thoughts.

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:22.720


00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:25.400
Link number 2 and link number 10,

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:30.480
these two are karma,

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:33.040
but different stages of karma.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:38.880
Number 2 is fresh karma, like a watermelon just planted.

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:45.880
Yes, and number 10 is ripe karma, the seeds are swollen and ready.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:49.520
Yes, okay, translate that while I drink my coffee.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:00.960
Then, he says a strange thing;

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:02.400
LHAG MA BDUN NI SDUG BSNGAL,

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.320
and the other seven,  they are suffering.

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:11.000
And then he quotes lu drup (KLU SGRUB),

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:14.000
Arya Nagarjuna.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:21.080
And this is by the way the same text on the essence of dependent origination

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:24.680
that we had before. It's very short. One or two pages.

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:39.600
So let's follow the Tibetan text because there are two interesting points here;

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:47.240
thang po gye pa gu nyon mong (DANG PO BRGYAD PA DGU NYON MONGS)

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.760
The first, eighth and nine

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:52.840
are negative thoughts,

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:56.400
the first, eighth and nine.

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:59.040
See,

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.080
he doesn't say the ninth.

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.880
He says nine, Nagarjuna.

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:14.400
Why didn't he say the ninth and just said nine?

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:21.880
Because, this is poetry, and he didn't have room to write the "-th".

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:30.560
So you won't get confused.

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:34.120
You should hear pa gu pa (PA, DGU PA).

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:38.480
Okay, now it should be clear, number 1, number 8, number 9, these three are negative emotions.

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:48.600
nye pa chu pa le yin  te (GNYIS PA BCU PA LAS YIN TE)

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:52.480
number 2 and number 10, these are the two karmas, these two are karmas.

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:57.760
hlak ma dun ni (LHAG MA BDUN NI)

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:02.120
now the remaining 7, the remaining 7,

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:05.960
duk ngel yin (SDUG BSNGAL YIN) - these are suffering.

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:10.760
Now, I always like to go back to the original text

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:17.000
at any point, this is the Mixed Nuts rule.

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:24.240
Whenever there is a quote in the book,

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:29.960
our translation team's rule is Mixed Nuts,

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:35.280
we are all the

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:39.080
reincarnations of Master Xuanzang's (XUANGZANG) students in the

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:44.120
Wild Goose Pagoda Tower during the time of Tangchao (TANGCHAO).

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:51.640
We have a rule,

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:56.960
if there is a quote, go and check it and make sure it is correct.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:07.160
So I checked it and then I told myself that it is correct.

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:11.680
Then I noticed that one word is different, the way

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:16.840
it is quoted in the lam  Rome, The

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:22.400
last line says LHAG MA BDUN NI,

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:26.800
which means the last, remaining seven,

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:31.760
they are suffering,

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:37.760
but it's a little uncomfortable, right? That is, the others must also be suffering, and the whole wheel is suffering.

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:50.280
The real ancient Tang Gyur (BSTANG 'GYUR) version of this verse

00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:59.200
says LHAG MA BDUN YANG

00:15:59.880 --> 00:16:00.760
not NI.

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:03.960
Okay, here, look here LHAG MA BDUN NI,

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:06.440
but it says LHAG MA BDUN YANG.

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:09.040
Which means the

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:12.440
remaining seven are also pain.

00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:21.120
So, I think everyone who has listened to this lesson up to this point,

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:31.080
I can accept that three of them are negative emotions - number one, eight and nine.

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:41.000
I can understand that two of them are karma - number two and ten.

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:48.040
But why does he say and the remaining seven are suffering?

00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:54.000
Why does he do this  says, aren't those first five suffering too?

00:16:57.920 --> 00:17:00.840
And if you thought of that when you heard me say it the first time,

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.160
you were right.

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:12.080
Because the original verse said the last seven are suffering too.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:23.880
So I did my third-grade drawing here;

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:37.040
I colored in around the first, eighth, and ninth links, which are the negative emotions.

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:44.040
Then in the next picture,

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:48.000
I colored in around numbers two and ten together.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:58.480
And then in the next picture, I colored in around three through seven and eleven – twelfth, those seven.

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:11.840
And of course, by now you know that those two groups are kind of the same thing.

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:19.920
3, 4, 5, 6,

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.200
7, and 11 and 12.

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:25.880
They're almost the same thing.

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:27.200
Why?

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:29.320
Number 3, my consciousness goes into my mom,

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:36.920
link number 4, my body and my consciousness are inside my mom,

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:43.760
link number 5, my eyes and ears and nose and so on grow inside my  moms.

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:52.160
link number 6 - they come into contact with the outside world,

00:18:56.240 --> 00:19:00.960
link number 7 - because of this contact, I have feelings, such as good feelings or bad feelings.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:07.320
3, 4, 5, 6, 7

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:12.440
but they are the same as 11 and 12.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:16.320
11 and 12 together are one whole human life.

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:24.880
I am born, I grow old, and I die.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:30.280
diy tsik kang thang po (DI'I TSIG RKANG DANG PO)

00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:33.040
so, these three pictures I made for you.

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:39.000
diy tsik kang thang poy the sum kun long thang (DI'I TSIG RKANG DANG PO'I DE GSUM KUN SLONG DANG)

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:43.000
He said something interesting

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:49.040
you can remember the first line of the verse, well

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:59.080
where Nagarjuna says that the first, and the eighth, and the ninth, they are negative emotions.

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:09.280
You can  think of them as the process of motivation to do something bad.

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:20.000
Then, you can remember the next stanza,

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:24.200
this next stanza says that number 2 and number 10 are karma.

00:20:27.640 --> 00:20:29.640
If you think about it,

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:32.560
number 2 and number 10,

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:38.440
they are karma expressed by you doing something or saying something.

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:47.760
Where is the mental karma?

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:53.040
He already talked about that in the first group. The

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:59.280
first group, those three mental obscurations are mental karma.

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:10.920
What does link number 1 and link number 2 mean?

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:17.200
Number 2, he says here,

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:23.400
must refer to the things you say and the things you do because of your bad motivation.

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:37.240
Why link 2, the potter, did he leave out the karma of thinking?

00:21:44.560 --> 00:21:49.000
Because that was already in the wrong understanding.

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:53.040
This is the karma of the mind.

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:55.960
Okay,

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:59.080
tsig kang sum pei the nam long cho yin (TSIG RKANG GSUM PA'I DE  RNAMS LONGS SPYOD YIN)

00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:05.000
Then, in the third line here, which says the other seven are suffering,

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:14.680
these links are just like what objects in your life that you cognize.

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:25.040


00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:27.280
If you reflect

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:30.000
on these 12 links;

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:34.120
what order they go in and how you stop them.

00:22:39.800 --> 00:22:42.360


00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:47.200
Then indeed, you automatically do the meditation on the pain of life.

00:22:54.760 --> 00:23:00.680
And then automatically there will be a shift in your heart.

00:23:03.560 --> 00:23:08.280
You will begin to understand, “Oh my god, I’m like a prisoner in this wheel,

00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:16.200
this world is a prison.”

00:23:17.760 --> 00:23:18.680
My life is a prison.

00:23:18.680 --> 00:23:20.800
And I’m doomed in this prison.

00:23:20.800 --> 00:23:22.800
My whole life I’ve been in prison. The

00:23:31.080 --> 00:23:33.720
only  The way to escape this prison is to die.

00:23:36.880 --> 00:23:38.880
And that's not a metaphor—that's reality.

00:23:42.040 --> 00:23:44.040
No matter how rich you are,

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:47.000
no matter how young you are,

00:23:48.800 --> 00:23:50.800
it doesn't matter,

00:23:51.440 --> 00:23:54.120
you're still locked in the prison of death.

00:24:02.600 --> 00:24:08.560
A. No. 1, you'd have to be crazy to think that all the people before you died, but you're not going to die.

00:24:18.720 --> 00:24:21.800
Then, if someone told you, you know, there's a pretty simple way to stop this problem,

00:24:29.040 --> 00:24:32.720
then I think you'd have to be crazy not to at least listen to them.

00:24:38.280 --> 00:24:41.400
So the whole idea—"my life is like a prison,"

00:24:41.680 --> 00:24:45.000
no matter what happens in my life, good or bad,

00:24:45.320 --> 00:24:48.640
I'm going to lose everything, even my life.

00:24:54.880 --> 00:24:59.880
Then, finally, you have this idea: "Oh, maybe there's a way I can get out."

00:25:00.240 --> 00:25:02.240
I mean, "I don't want to die,

00:25:02.600 --> 00:25:06.040
but I would like to change my life and make it like heaven.

00:25:14.960 --> 00:25:17.800
I would like that.

00:25:18.200 --> 00:25:20.880
Then he says nge jung yin (NGES 'BYUNG YIN)

00:25:21.480 --> 00:25:24.440
this is renunciation.

00:25:27.440 --> 00:25:33.280
In English, the word renunciation, especially by waiters and restaurateurs, was never used.

00:25:40.040 --> 00:25:44.880
Even in the ancient Christian tradition, where this word came from,

00:25:51.000 --> 00:25:56.600
it means that I will stay in the monastery, I will eat simple food, I will have a simple bed, something like that.

00:26:04.400 --> 00:26:08.360
But the word in Buddhism, the original word is nge jung (NGES ' BYUNG)

00:26:14.480 --> 00:26:17.760
it feels different and has a different meaning.

00:26:19.880 --> 00:26:25.040
Of course, all of you who have studied the ACI courses know that this is the first of the three main paths,

00:26:33.880 --> 00:26:37.280
and it is very simple to explain -

00:26:37.440 --> 00:26:39.680
it simply means, I want to get out of here!

00:26:43.320 --> 00:26:48.240
This does not mean what the Christian word "renunciation" means.  This is not what is meant.

00:26:54.080 --> 00:27:00.320
This doesn't mean I'm going to avoid fine dining, or not go on vacation, or not watch movies.

00:27:08.320 --> 00:27:11.600
In Buddhism, nge jung (NGES ' BYUNG) means I definitely want to get out of here.

00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:19.360
So your life from the moment you are born

00:27:19.480 --> 00:27:22.680
, from the minute you are born until the minute you die, it is

00:27:26.160 --> 00:27:29.000
all exactly the same as a prison.

00:27:33.280 --> 00:27:38.440
When you say, "This guy is rich," you simply mean that this guy has more money in his prison cell,

00:27:39.040 --> 00:27:41.040
which is the same cell I am in.

00:27:50.160 --> 00:27:52.160
Or "that movie star is very beautiful,"

00:27:54.040 --> 00:28:00.600
but that just means she's in the same prison cell as me and she's going to lose all her beauty too.

00:28:12.520 --> 00:28:18.080
I don't see that the word "renunciation" means a gloomy person who is ordained to the priesthood.

00:28:29.360 --> 00:28:32.680
In many religious traditions, including Buddhism,

00:28:35.680 --> 00:28:37.920


00:28:38.800 --> 00:28:40.360
the image of renunciation in your mind

00:28:41.920 --> 00:28:44.560
is of a monk or nun who is not particularly happy.

00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:52.800
They won't eat donuts because they taste good.

00:28:56.080 --> 00:28:59.000
You don't think about anyone happy.

00:29:03.640 --> 00:29:07.120
But what we were talking about today is

00:29:08.440 --> 00:29:11.400
if you achieve true renunciation

00:29:12.600 --> 00:29:15.080
it's something like Steve Jobs or something like that.

00:29:17.640 --> 00:29:20.840
It means you're really excited about a new idea, that's all.

00:29:23.600 --> 00:29:29.040
It's like a new vision, what's that guy's name, Elon Musk

00:29:30.200 --> 00:29:32.200
Yeah, let's make a new spaceship,

00:29:34.120 --> 00:29:36.040
let's make a new kind of car.

00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:38.800
And renunciation should be exactly like this

00:29:40.440 --> 00:29:44.320
Yes, that's right, let's get out of this shitty world, let's make a cool world.

00:29:47.360 --> 00:29:49.360
Yes, we could do that.

00:29:52.040 --> 00:29:53.600
It's like... I don't know...

00:29:54.560 --> 00:29:56.560
Elon Musk doesn't want to drive a car that pollutes the entire planet,

00:30:07.280 --> 00:30:11.040
he has some kind of positive, happy, cool vision.

00:30:16.120 --> 00:30:18.440
Yeah, let's get rid of these stinking cars,

00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:24.280
everyone will get a Tesla, and then the whole world will be clean.

00:30:29.000 --> 00:30:32.000
This is what renunciation should taste like.

00:30:34.960 --> 00:30:37.280
I want a cool world, I don't want this stupid world.

00:30:40.800 --> 00:30:41.440
Grow old,

00:30:42.440 --> 00:30:45.160
shrivel up like an old monkey,

00:30:47.160 --> 00:30:49.320
then lose teeth, then die, you know.

00:30:52.160 --> 00:30:53.160
This is not cool

00:30:54.000 --> 00:30:56.320
I want something cool.

00:30:56.320 --> 00:30:59.640
Okay, so experience this feeling about renunciation.

00:31:01.480 --> 00:31:03.400
I don't know, but you probably felt that

00:31:06.040 --> 00:31:07.800
here the lamrim

00:31:08.560 --> 00:31:10.120
shifts away

00:31:11.200 --> 00:31:13.920
from explaining the problem.

00:31:16.120 --> 00:31:17.280
And you might have felt something like this

00:31:17.280 --> 00:31:20.080
Elon Musk vibe of

00:31:21.680 --> 00:31:25.040
"Oh, we'll have a solution soon..."

